v2-bootstrap: close the six review minors on the reuse controls (PATCH 5)

Six corrections from the independent source reviews, all in the claim file:

1. The real-producer citation was wrong. walk_population_controls holds
   check-layout over the live roots and walks parse-population over the FIXTURE
   roots only; the lookup over the repository runs in the gate's parse-verdict
   steps, and the publishing walk's Reused arm only once witnesses.yml carries
   --reuse-from. Corrected at all three sites, including the footer obligation.
2. judge_read's comment now describes what it does: a parses row goes standing
   then counted then acceptance, and a refused row skips BOTH (fixture refusal
   rows carry no digest, so standing cannot be judged). No production counting
   was changed for prose.
3. Added a_declared_refused_member_is_demoted_and_publishes_nothing: member_file
   declared refused, base holding its own line, parsable content through
   population_parse_member_decided, asserting miss_declared_refused=1, reused=0,
   parsed=0, one refusal and no receipt. This is the combined standing/counting/
   refusal route, previously covered only in pieces.
4. Two mutation rows relabelled rather than claimed: publishing under another
   member's key is UNOBSERVABLE at this interface (the line carries no key), and
   using the base's line is an EQUIVALENT mutation (Reused requires the exact
   recomputed line).
5. Stated at suite grain which controls a parser that refuses everything would
   satisfy, and which three require a member to parse.
6. enumerate_bound_modules named where the text said "the roster enumeration".

Comment-only plus one new test fn; no production behaviour changed. Nothing
executed: no CI job runs witnesses, so every claim here stays a source review.
